/target
# A second build directory, for building while a long run holds the first
# one's binaries open. Windows will not let cargo replace a running exe.
/target-alt

# Console BIOS images. SCPH-xxxx BIOS dumps are copyrighted Sony code and can
# never be committed, in any region or revision. Bring your own dump; the
# tracked bios/README.md says which ones the core expects and how it checks them.
/bios/*
!/bios/README.md

# Commercial disc images, PSX-EXE test binaries, save states, memory cards,
# classifier output: ALL of it stays out of git. Blanket-ignore the whole
# dumps/ tree so no copyrighted image can be committed regardless of subfolder.
/dumps/*
!/dumps/README.md

# Hardware documentation. Third-party reference material (MIPS R3000 manuals,
# Sony service manuals, psx-spx mirrors) is not ours to redistribute, even when
# it is freely available. So under docs/ only **markdown** is tracked: our own
# notes, and the derived reference write-ups in docs/ref/ that cite their
# sources rather than reproducing them. Raw drops of any other kind (PDF, HTML,
# archives) can land anywhere in here and stay untracked.
#
# If a verbatim third-party document ever arrives *as* markdown, it does not
# belong in git either. Distil it and cite it, the same way docs/ref/ does.
/docs/**
!/docs/**/
!/docs/**/*.md

# Vendored third-party test suites (ps1-tests and friends): binaries plus their
# reference logs. Not ours to redistribute, and large. Bring your own, the same
# way FamiRust treats the TomHarte vectors. `testrom --dir` walks whatever path
# it is given, so nothing here is load-bearing for the build.
/tests/

# Headless render / audio / TTY dumps from the dev harnesses.
/out/

# Local convenience junction -> TrophyHubAndroid app jniLibs (deploy target)
android-jnilibs/

# Scratch from RSTA_GTE_TRACE runs.
trace.log
sio.log
/target-*/
